.TH XUR.STD.RE.DOTNET.RUNTIME 7 "2026-10-27" "xur 0.1.1" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.re.dotnet.runtime \- host a .NET runtime
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::re::dotnet::runtime
starts and drives a .NET runtime (CoreCLR) from Xur.
Assemblies can be loaded from disk and methods called by looking up
their native function pointers.
.PP
Backed by
.BR hao\-runtime .
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B coreclr()
Start the CoreCLR runtime, or return the one already running.
Only one CoreCLR can exist per process.
Returns
.BR Result<Runtime,\ str> .
.SH Runtime METHODS
.TP
.B backend()
The active backend name:
.B \(dqCoreClr\(dq
or
.BR \(dqMono\(dq .
.TP
.B load_assembly(path)
Load a .NET assembly from disk and make it available by name.
Returns
.BR Result<(),\ str> .
.TP
.B function_pointer(assembly, type, method)
Get a native function pointer to a static
.B [UnmanagedCallersOnly]
method.
Returns
.BR Result<int,\ str> .
.TP
.B method_pointer(assembly, type, method)
Get a JIT-compiled function pointer to any static method, whether or
not it is
.BR [UnmanagedCallersOnly] .
Returns
.BR Result<int,\ str> .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.nf
use std::re::dotnet::runtime;

fn main() -> Result<(), str> {
    let rt = runtime::coreclr()?;
    rt.load_assembly("MyLib.dll")?;
    let fp = rt.function_pointer(
        "MyLib", "MyClass", "MyMethod"
    )?;
    io::println("pointer: 0x{}", fp.to_hex());
    Ok(())
}
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur (1),
.BR xur.std.re (7),
.BR xur.std.re.dotnet.il2cpp (7)
